{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Python code to GNU C++11 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Python 2 code to GNU C++11 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Python 2 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n<your_rewritten_code_4>\nimport sys\n\ndef main():\n    # Read input\n    line = sys.stdin.readline()\n    n, h = map(int, line.split())\n    \n    # Initialize dp array\n    dp = [[-1 for _ in range(n + 1)] for __ in range(n + 1)]\n    dp[0][0] = 1\n    \n    # Define recursive function with memoization\n    def f(n_val, h_val):\n        if dp[n_val][h_val] != -1:\n            return dp[n_val][h_val]\n        \n        if n_val == 0:\n            dp[n_val][h_val] = 0\n            return 0\n        if h_val == 0:\n            dp[n_val][h_val] = f(n_val, 1)\n            return dp[n_val][h_val]\n        \n        result = 0\n        for i in range(n_val):\n            result += f(n_val - i - 1, 0) * f(i, h_val - 1)\n            result += f(n_val - i - 1, h_val - 1) * f(i, 0)\n            result -= f(n_val - i - 1, h_val - 1) * f(i, h_val - 1)\n        \n        dp[n_val][h_val] = result\n        return result\n    \n    # Compute and print result\n    output = f(n, h)\n    print output\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n</your_rewritten_code_4>\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <string>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    string line;\n    getline(cin, line);\n    int n, h;\n    {\n        size_t pos1 = line.find(' ');\n        n = stoi(line.substr(0, pos1));\n        h = stoi(line.substr(pos1 + 1));\n    }\n    \n    vector<vector<long long>> dp(n + 1, vector<long long>(n + 1, -1));\n    dp[0][0] = 1;\n    \n    // Recursive function with memoization using lambda\n    function<long long(int, int)> f = [&](int n_val, int h_val) -> long long {\n        if (dp[n_val][h_val] != -1) {\n            return dp[n_val][h_val];\n        }\n        \n        if (n_val == 0) {\n            dp[n_val][h_val] = 0;\n            return 0;\n        }\n        if (h_val == 0) {\n            dp[n_val][h_val] = f(n_val, 1);\n            return dp[n_val][h_val];\n        }\n        \n        long long result = 0;\n        for (int i = 0; i < n_val; i++) {\n            result += f(n_val - i - 1, 0) * f(i, h_val - 1);\n            result += f(n_val - i - 1, h_val - 1) * f(i, 0);\n            result -= f(n_val - i - 1, h_val - 1) * f(i, h_val - 1);\n        }\n        \n        dp[n_val][h_val] = result;\n        return result;\n    };\n    \n    long long output = f(n, h);\n    cout << output << endl;\n    \n    return 0;\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-8.725739462533966e-05, -5.483612312673358e-06, -8.344646857949556e-07, -0.00014911970356479287, -7.152555099310121e-07, -0.0001433984871255234, -2.264974000354414e-06, -4.768360213347478e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.0014860312221571803, -0.0019296851241961122, -0.14268697798252106, -4.410734163684538e-06, -0.3664533197879791, -0.6932717561721802, -0.5759920477867126, -1.9430925021879375e-05, -1.9073468138230965e-06, -5.960462772236497e-07, -0.5777249932289124, -0.006074656266719103